  fmpq_gcd(gq, Nq, Cq) against fmpq_gcd(gq, Cq, Nq): the gcd of (p, q) and (r, s) is the canonical form of gcd(p s, q r)/(q s), which is symmetric in the two arguments (refs/src/flint-3.0.1/fmpq.rst:509-514); gq is a temporary, so no input is written

EXCUSED src/cap.c:169:5 swap_args: 'adf_fball_mul(t, x, y)' -> 'adf_fball_mul(t, y, x)'
  adf_fball_mul computes the tight set product with radius gcd(a M, b N, N M) (docs/proofs/precision.md Proposition 2, line 34), symmetric in (a, N) and (b, M); the local branch tests gcd(gcd(r_i, s_i), q_i) and multiplies the denominators and the residues, all symmetric, and the global one is fb_mul_global (src/fball.c:715-745, 762-808), so the same ball is written; the output may be an input (include/adelefeld/fball.h:23)

