EXCUSED src/cap.c:133:5 swap_args: 'adf_fball_add(t, x, y)' -> 'adf_fball_add(t, y, x)'
  adf_fball_add computes the set sum (a + N Zhat) + (b + M Zhat) = (a + b) + gcd(N, M) Zhat (docs/proofs/precision.md Proposition 1, line 27) in every branch, with the same backend test for both orders (fb_same_local is symmetric), the local sum through the lcm of the two denominators and the global one through fmpq_add and fmpq_gcd (src/fball.c:201-224, 600-628), so the same ball is written; the output may be an input (include/adelefeld/fball.h:23)

